<!-- RAASI INTRO -->
<section class="raasi-intro-section">
  <div class="section-label">What is Raasi?</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Your Moon Sign —<br/>your <em>inner world</em></h2>
  <div class="raasi-intro-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="raasi-intro-body">In Vedic astrology, your <strong>Raasi</strong> (Moon Sign) is determined by where the Moon was positioned in the zodiac at the moment of your birth. Unlike Western astrology, which emphasizes the Sun Sign, Vedic astrology considers the Moon Sign to be the primary indicator of your emotional nature, mental tendencies, and subconscious patterns.</p>
      <p class="raasi-intro-body">Your Raasi governs how you feel, how you process emotions, how you relate to your family and home, and what brings you inner peace or distress. It is your emotional blueprint — the part of you that others may not see on the surface but that shapes every decision you make.</p>
      <div class="raasi-intro-highlight">
        <div class="raasi-intro-highlight-title">Why Raasi Matters</div>
        <p class="raasi-intro-highlight-text">Two people with the same Sun Sign (like Aries in Western astrology) can have very different Raasis — one might be Meenam (emotionally sensitive, intuitive) and the other Mesham (emotionally driven, impulsive). This distinction shapes how they experience life at a fundamental level.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="raasi-intro-body">There are 12 Raasis in the Vedic zodiac, each with its own elemental nature, ruling planet, and karmic themes. Scroll down to explore all 12.</p>
    </div>
